tate.json" "file_sha256" "c674633b21c6588b958297ac2f06835b9cdc61ec31fc9669ff000f9e8e7d917e"} {"question" "q-282146" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0118fa4be877af9d984d96913b8c4eb3649797d2aa3621bd31fccb9b4080a716"} {"question" "q-282146" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/state.json" "file_sha256" "c674633b21c6588b958297ac2f06835b9cdc61ec31fc9669ff000f9e8e7d917e"} {"question" "q-282146" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "30"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/state.json" "file_sha256" "c674633b21c6588b958297ac2f06835b9cdc61ec31fc9669ff000f9e8e7d917e"} {"question" "q-282146" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/state.json" "file_sha256" "c674633b21c6588b958297ac2f06835b9cdc61ec31fc9669ff000f9e8e7d917e"} {"question" "q-282146" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "32"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/state.json" "file_sha256" "c674633b21c6588b958297ac2f06835b9cdc61ec31fc9669ff000f9e8e7d917e"} {"question" "q-282146" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/state.json" "file_sha256" "c674633b21c6588b958297ac2f06835b9cdc61ec31fc9669ff000f9e8e7d917e"} {"question" "q-282146" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "41"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/state.json" "file_sha256" "c674633b21c6588b958297ac2f06835b9cdc61ec31fc9669ff000f9e8e7d917e"} {"question" "q-103542" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨-1,2x,3⟩,$ $b=⟨2,-x,1⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{355}.$ Find $x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/state.json" "file_sha256" "c674633b21c6588b958297ac2f06835b9cdc61ec31fc9669ff000f9e8e7d917e"} {"question" "q-103542" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 2x & 3 \\\\ 2 & -x & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2x & 3 \\\\ -x & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2x \\\\ 2 & -x\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2x+3x)i-(-1-6)j+(x-4x)k \\\\  & =⟨5x,7,-3x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(5x)^{2}+(7)^{2}+(-3x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25{x}^{2}+49+9{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{34{x}^{2}+49}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{355} \\\\ \\sqrt{34{x}^{2}+49} & =\\sqrt{355} \\\\ 34{x}^{2}+49 & =355 \\\\ 34{x}^{2} & =306 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=\\pm 3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/state.json" "file_sha256" "c674633b21c6588b958297ac2f06835b9cdc61ec31fc9669ff000f9e8e7d917e"} {"question" "q-103542" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0118fa4be877af9d984d96913b8c4eb3649797d2aa3621bd31fccb9b4080a716"} {"question" "q-103542" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/state.json" "file_sha256" "c674633b21c6588b958297ac2f06835b9cdc61ec31fc9669ff000f9e8e7d917e"} {"question" "q-103542" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=-3,9"] ["math" "x=-\\frac{1}{3},3"] ["math" "x=\\pm 3"] ["math" "x=\\pm 9"] ["math" "x=\\pm \\frac{1}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/state.json" "file_sha256" "c674633b21c6588b958297ac2f06835b9cdc61ec31fc9669ff000f9e8e7d917e"} {"question" "q-103542" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=\\pm 3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/state.json" "file_sha256" "c674633b21c6588b958297ac2f06835b9cdc61ec31fc9669ff000f9e8e7d917e"} {"question" "q-282269" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨x,1,1⟩,$ $b=⟨1,0,3⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{10}.$ Find $x.$\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/state.json" "file_sha256" "c674633b21c6588b958297ac2f06835b9cdc61ec31fc9669ff000f9e8e7d917e"} {"question" "q-282269" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ x & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}x & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}x & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3-0)i-(3x-1)j+(0-1)k \\\\  & =⟨3,1-3x,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(1-3x)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+(9{x}^{2}-6x+1)+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{x}^{2}-6x+11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{10} \\\\ \\sqrt{9{x}^{2}-6x+11} & =\\sqrt{10} \\\\ 9{x}^{2}-6x+11 & =10 \\\\ (3x-1)^{2} & =0 \\\\ 3x-1 & =0 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=\\frac{1}{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/state.json" "file_sha256" "c674633b21c6588b958297ac2f06835b9cdc61ec31fc9669ff000f9e8e7d917e"} {"question" "q-282269" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0118fa4be877af9d984d96913b8c4eb3649797d2aa3621bd31fccb9b4080a716"} {"question" "q-282269" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/state.json" "file_sha256" "c674633b21c6588b958297ac2f06835b9cdc61ec31fc9669ff000f9e8e7d917e"} {"question" "q-282269" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/state.json" "file_sha256" "c674633b21c6588b958297ac2f06835b9cdc61ec31fc9669ff000f9e8e7d917e"} {"question" "q-282262" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨x,3,0⟩,$ $b=⟨-x,0,1⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{49}.$ Then, in **ascending order**, the possible values of $x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/state.json" "file_sha256" "c674633b21c6588b958297ac2f06835b9cdc61ec31fc9669ff000f9e8e7d917e"} {"question" "q-282262" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ x & 3 & 0 \\\\ -x & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}x & 0 \\\\ -x & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}x & 3 \\\\ -x & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3-0)i-(x+0)j+(0+3x)k \\\\  & =⟨3,-x,3x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-x)^{2}+(3x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+{x}^{2}+9{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10{x}^{2}+9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{49} \\\\ \\sqrt{10{x}^{2}+9} & =\\sqrt{49} \\\\ 10{x}^{2}+9 & =49 \\\\ 10{x}^{2} & =40 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=-2,$ $x=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/state.json" "file_sha256" "c674633b21c6588b958297ac2f06835b9cdc61ec31fc9669ff000f9e8e7d917e"} {"question" "q-282262" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0118fa4be877af9d984d96913b8c4eb3649797d2aa3621bd31fccb9b4080a716"} {"question" "q-282262" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/state.json" "file_sha256" "c674633b21c6588b958297ac2f06835b9cdc61ec31fc9669ff000f9e8e7d917e"} {"question" "q-282262" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/state.json" "file_sha256" "c674633b21c6588b958297ac2f06835b9cdc61ec31fc9669ff000f9e8e7d917e"} {"question" "q-282262" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/state.json" "file_sha256" "c674633b21c6588b958297ac2f06835b9cdc61ec31fc9669ff000f9e8e7d917e"} {"question" "q-282262" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/state.json" "file_sha256" "c674633b21c6588b958297ac2f06835b9cdc61ec31fc9669ff000f9e8e7d917e"} {"question" "q-103540" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨2x,3,2⟩$, $b=⟨x,1,-1⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{93}.$ Find $x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/state.json" "file_sha256" "c674633b21c6588b958297ac2f06835b9cdc61ec31fc9669ff000f9e8e7d917e"} {"question" "q-103540" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2x & 3 & 2 \\\\ x & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2x & 2 \\\\ x & -1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2x & 3 \\\\ x & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(-3-2)i-(-2x-2x)j+(2x-3x)k \\\\  & =⟨-5,-4x,x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(-5)^{2}+(-4x)^{2}+{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25+16{x}^{2}+{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{17{x}^{2}+25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{93} \\\\ \\sqrt{17{x}^{2}+25} & =\\sqrt{93} \\\\ 17{x}^{2}+25 & =93 \\\\ 17{x}^{2} & =68 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=\\pm 2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/state.json" "file_sha256" "c674633b21c6588b958297ac2f06835b9cdc61ec31fc9669ff000f9e8e7d917e"} {"question" "q-103540" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0118fa4be877af9d984d96913b8c4eb3649797d2aa3621bd31fccb9b4080a716"} {"question" "q-103540" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/state.json" "file_sha256" "c674633b21c6588b958297ac2f06835b9cdc61ec31fc9669ff000f9e8e7d917e"} {"question" "q-103540" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=-2,4"] ["math" "x=-4,2"] ["math" "x=4"] ["math" "x=\\pm 2"] ["math" "x=\\pm 4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/state.json" "file_sha256" "c674633b21c6588b958297ac2f06835b9cdc61ec31fc9669ff000f9e8e7d917e"} {"question" "q-103540" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=\\pm 2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/state.json" "file_sha256" "c674633b21c6588b958297ac2f06835b9cdc61ec31fc9669ff000f9e8e7d917e"} {"question" "q-282260" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨2x,3,1⟩,$ $b=⟨-2x,0,4⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{280}.$ Then, in **ascending order**, the possible values of $x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/state.json" "file_sha256" "c674633b21c6588b958297ac2f06835b9cdc61ec31fc9669ff000f9e8e7d917e"} {"question" "q-282260" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2x & 3 & 1 \\\\ -2x & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2x & 1 \\\\ -2x & 4\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2x & 3 \\\\ -2x & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(12-0)i-(8x+2x)j+(0+6x)k \\\\  & =⟨12,-10x,6x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{12}^{2}+(-10x)^{2}+(6x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{144+100{x}^{2}+36{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{136{x}^{2}+144}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{280} \\\\ \\sqrt{136{x}^{2}+144} & =\\sqrt{280} \\\\ 136{x}^{2}+144 & =280 \\\\ 136{x}^{2} & =136 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=-1,$ $x=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/state.json" "file_sha256" "c674633b21c6588b958297ac2f06835b9cdc61ec31fc9669ff000f9e8e7d917e"} {"question" "q-282260" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0118fa4be877af9d984d96913b8c4eb3649797d2aa3621bd31fccb9b4080a716"} {"question" "q-282260" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/state.json" "file_sha256" "c674633b21c6588b958297ac2f06835b9cdc61ec31fc9669ff000f9e8e7d917e"} {"question" "q-282260" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/state.json" "file_sha256" "c674633b21c6588b958297ac2f06835b9cdc61ec31fc9669ff000f9e8e7d917e"} {"question" "q-282260" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/state.json" "file_sha256" "c674633b21c6588b958297ac2f06835b9cdc61ec31fc9669ff000f9e8e7d917e"} {"question" "q-282260" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/state.json" "file_sha256" "c674633b21c6588b958297ac2f06835b9cdc61ec31fc9669ff000f9e8e7d917e"} {"question" "e-4341" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 3,-4,1 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle -7,0,2 \\rangle.$ Find $\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/example-4341.json" "file_sha256" "5b668d7430ddd4c028760aa614195673a81303fedb7034b9cb195a85b17410e3"} {"question" "e-4341" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -7 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 \\\\ -7 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-4)\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 0)i-(3\\cdot 2-1\\cdot (-7))j+(3\\cdot 0-(-4)\\cdot (-7))k \\\\  & =-8i-13j-28k \\\\  & =⟨-8,-13,-28⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/example-4341.json" "file_sha256" "5b668d7430ddd4c028760aa614195673a81303fedb7034b9cb195a85b17410e3"} {"question" "e-4343" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 3, 1, 2x \\rangle,$ $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 0,1,x \\rangle,$ and $|\\,\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}\\,| = \\sqrt{19}.$ Find $x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/example-4343.json" "file_sha256" "5b1ad67bf4163862d73eb7ca033ee82505799922d4112761bee1e65679443669"} {"question" "e-4343" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2x \\\\ 0 & 1 & x\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2x \\\\ 1 & x\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2x \\\\ 0 & x\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =-xi-3xj+3k \\\\  & =⟨-x,-3x,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(-x)^{2}+(-3x)^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10{x}^{2}+9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & |\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{19} \\\\  & \\sqrt{10{x}^{2}+9}=\\sqrt{19} \\\\  & 10{x}^{2}+9=19 \\\\  & 10{x}^{2}=10 \\\\  & {x}^{2}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x= \\pm 1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039715/example-4343.json" "file_sha256" "5b1ad67bf4163862d73eb7ca033ee82505799922d4112761bee1e65679443669"}] "usage" {"e-4341" [] "e-4343" []} "basis" 1375 "retractions" [[17592186059469 :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 3,-4,1 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle -7,0,2 \\rangle$. Find $\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}$."] [17592186059469 :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}\\mathbf{a} \\times  \\mathbf{b} & = \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{ccc}\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 3 & - 4 & 1 \\\\ - 7 & 0 & 2\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\\\  & = \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}- 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\mathbf{i} - \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}3 & 1 \\\\ - 7 & 2\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\mathbf{j} + \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}3 & - 4 \\\\ - 7 & 0\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\mathbf{k} \\\\  & = ( ( - 4 ) \\cdot  2 - 1 \\cdot  0 ) \\mathbf{i} - ( 3 \\cdot  2 - 1 \\cdot  ( - 7 ) ) \\mathbf{j} + ( 3 \\cdot  0 - ( - 4 ) \\cdot  ( - 7 ) ) \\mathbf{k} \\\\  & = - 8 \\mathbf{i} - 13 \\mathbf{j} - 28 \\mathbf{k} \\\\  & = \\langle  - 8 , - 13 , - 28 \\rangle  .\\end{array}$$"] [17592186059470 :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 3, 1, 2x \\rangle$, $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 0,1,x \\rangle$, and $\\mid \\,\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}\\, \\mid = \\sqrt{19}$. Find $x$."] [17592186059470 :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}\\mathbf{a} \\times  \\mathbf{b} & = \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{ccc}\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 x \\\\ 0 & 1 & x\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\\\  & = \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}1 & 2 x \\\\ 1 & x\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\mathbf{i} - \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}3 & 2 x \\\\ 0 & x\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\mathbf{j} + \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\mathbf{k} \\\\  & = - x \\mathbf{i} - 3 x \\mathbf{j} + 3 \\mathbf{k} \\\\  & = \\langle  - x , - 3 x , 3 \\rangle  .\\end{array}$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}| \\, \\mathbf{a} \\times  \\mathbf{b} \\, | & = \\sqrt{( - x {)}^{2} + ( - 3 x {)}^{2} + {3}^{2}} \\\\  & = \\sqrt{10 {x}^{2} + 9} .\\end{array}$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl} & | \\, \\mathbf{a} \\times  \\mathbf{b} \\, | = \\sqrt{19} \\\\  & \\sqrt{10 {x}^{2} + 9} = \\sqrt{19} \\\\  & 10 {x}^{2} + 9 = 19 \\\\  & 10 {x}^{2} = 10 \\\\  & {x}^{2} = 1\\end{array}$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x= \\pm 1$."]] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
